Streamed UTF-8 gets corrupted at chunk boundaries. Save /workspace/chunks.mjs:

export function decodeChunks(buffers) {
  // buffers: array of Buffer chunks from a network stream
  let out = "";
  for (const b of buffers) out += b.toString("utf8");
  return out;
}

If a multi-byte character is split across two chunks, each half decodes to U+FFFD garbage. Reproduce first in chunks.test.mjs (node:test): take const buf = Buffer.from('héllo 🌍 wörld', 'utf8'), split it at EVERY byte offset into two chunks, and assert decodeChunks([a, b]) equals the original string for all split points; run it and show the failures at offsets inside the multi-byte characters. Then fix using string_decoder's StringDecoder (write each chunk, plus decoder.end()), rerun the exhaustive split test until green, and add a three-chunk split that lands both boundaries inside the emoji's four bytes.

